      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023-sch-1-sec-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1 Subsection 51B(1)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023#sch-1-sec-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n(1) If:\n(a) a person commences to provide a designated service; and\n(b) the person’s name is not entered on the Reporting Entities\nRoll;\nthe person must, no later than 28 days after the day on which the\nperson commences to provide the designated service, apply under\nsubsection 51E(1) for enrolment as a reporting entity.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n(1) If:\n(a) a person commences to provide a designated service; and\n(b) the person’s name is not entered on the Reporting Entities\nRoll;\nthe person must, no later than 28 days after the day on which the\nperson commences to provide the designated service, apply under\nsubsection 51E(1) for enrolment as a reporting entity.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023-sch-1-sec-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023-sch-1-sec-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "92a70b7103282c153980a5ccd53ff7ed26f0b0e00b8d9aa873fe8a980ef649ee",
      "skos:note": "Must apply for enrolment as a reporting entity within 28 days of providing a designated service.",
      "dc:description": "Enrolment application under subsection 51E(1)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023#sch-1-sec-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1 Subsection 51B(1)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n(1) If:\n(a) a person commences to provide a designated service; and\n(b) the person’s name is not entered on the Reporting Entities\nRoll;\nthe person must, no later than 28 days after the day on which the\nperson commences to provide the designated service, apply under\nsubsection 51E(1) for enrolment as a reporting entity."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023-sch-1-sec-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023-sch-1-sec-1"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023-sch-1-sec-1-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to apply for enrolment",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023-sch-1-sec-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "2 After subsection 51B(2)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023#sch-1-sec-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n(2A) Subsection (1) does not apply if, when the person commences to\nprovide the designated service, the person is already required under\nthat subsection to apply for enrolment because of the provision of\nanother designated service.\nContinuing obligation to enrol\n(2B) If:\n(a) a person is required under subsection (1) of this section to\napply for enrolment by a particular time; and\n(b) the person does not apply for enrolment by that time;\nthen the obligation to apply for enrolment continues until:\n(c) the person applies for enrolment; or\n(d) the person ceases to be a reporting entity;\nwhichever occurs first.\n\nAnti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing Act 2006  Schedule 1\nFailure to enrol  Part 1\nNo. 63, 2023\nCrimes and Other Legislation Amendment (Omnibus) Act 2023\nMultiple contraventions\n(2C) A person who contravenes subsection (1) by failing to apply for\nenrolment as a reporting entity by a particular time (the enrolment\ndeadline) is taken to commit a separate contravention of that\nsubsection on each day that occurs:\n(a) on or after the day on which the enrolment deadline occurs;\nand\n(b) on or before the day on which the person’s obligation to\napply for enrolment ends (see subsection (2B)).\n(2D) To avoid doubt, a person does not contravene subsection (1) more\nthan once on any particular day, even if the person commences to\nprovide a designated service more than once on a particular day or\nduring a particular period.",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n(2A) Subsection (1) does not apply if, when the person commences to\nprovide the designated service, the person is already required under\nthat subsection to apply for enrolment because of the provision of\nanother designated service.\nContinuing obligation to enrol\n(2B) If:\n(a) a person is required under subsection (1) of this section to\napply for enrolment by a particular time; and\n(b) the person does not apply for enrolment by that time;\nthen the obligation to apply for enrolment continues until:\n(c) the person applies for enrolment; or\n(d) the person ceases to be a reporting entity;\nwhichever occurs first.\n\nAnti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing Act 2006  Schedule 1\nFailure to enrol  Part 1\nNo. 63, 2023\nCrimes and Other Legislation Amendment (Omnibus) Act 2023\nMultiple contraventions\n(2C) A person who contravenes subsection (1) by failing to apply for\nenrolment as a reporting entity by a particular time (the enrolment\ndeadline) is taken to commit a separate contravention of that\nsubsection on each day that occurs:\n(a) on or after the day on which the enrolment deadline occurs;\nand\n(b) on or before the day on which the person’s obligation to\napply for enrolment ends (see subsection (2B)).\n(2D) To avoid doubt, a person does not contravene subsection (1) more\nthan once on any particular day, even if the person commences to\nprovide a designated service more than once on a particular day or\nduring a particular period.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023-sch-1-sec-2-ss-2a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023-sch-1-sec-2-ss-2b"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023-sch-1-sec-2-ss-2c"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023-sch-1-sec-2-ss-2d"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8445d5cfe714f4491bdd7be3a32948e53e2a96ef2d6d75ca8d501fbc73a359c4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023#sch-1-sec-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2 After subsection 51B(2)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n(2A) Subsection (1) does not apply if, when the person commences to\nprovide the designated service, the person is already required under\nthat subsection to apply for enrolment because of the provision of\nanother designated service.\nContinuing obligation to enrol\n(2B) If:\n(a) a person is required under subsection (1) of this section to\napply for enrolment by a particular time; and\n(b) the person does not apply for enrolment by that time;\nthen the obligation to apply for enrolment continues until:\n(c) the person applies for enrolment; or\n(d) the person ceases to be a reporting entity;\nwhichever occurs first.\n\nAnti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing Act 2006  Schedule 1\nFailure to enrol  Part 1\nNo. 63, 2023\nCrimes and Other Legislation Amendment (Omnibus) Act 2023\nMultiple contraventions\n(2C) A person who contravenes subsection (1) by failing to apply for\nenrolment as a reporting entity by a particular time (the enrolment\ndeadline) is taken to commit a separate contravention of that\nsubsection on each day that occurs:\n(a) on or after the day on which the enrolment deadline occurs;\nand\n(b) on or before the day on which the person’s obligation to\napply for enrolment ends (see subsection (2B)).\n(2D) To avoid doubt, a person does not contravene subsection (1) more\nthan once on any particular day, even if the person commences to\nprovide a designated service more than once on a particular day or\nduring a particular period."
    },
