    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023-sch-6-sec-24a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "24A Decision by the Attorney-General to refuse consent to transfer",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023#sch-6-sec-24a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023.pdf, p.23",
      "values:originalText": "to Australia\n(1) The Attorney-General may decide to refuse consent to the transfer\nof a prisoner to Australia under this Part:\n(a) after the Attorney-General receives a request under\nsection 24 for the transfer; but\n(b) before the Attorney-General has started to act under any of\nsections 26 to 32 in relation to the transfer.\n(2) Sections 26 to 32 do not apply for the transfer of the prisoner if the\nAttorney-General decides under subsection (1) of this section to\nrefuse consent to the transfer.",
      "skos:definition": "to Australia\n(1) The Attorney-General may decide to refuse consent to the transfer\nof a prisoner to Australia under this Part:\n(a) after the Attorney-General receives a request under\nsection 24 for the transfer; but\n(b) before the Attorney-General has started to act under any of\nsections 26 to 32 in relation to the transfer.\n(2) Sections 26 to 32 do not apply for the transfer of the prisoner if the\nAttorney-General decides under subsection (1) of this section to\nrefuse consent to the transfer.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023-sch-6-sec-24a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023-sch-6-sec-24a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4944190fe428597b7d9314d10c2da5fed1f17f62835b8b9c5bf10daffb3a4c43"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023#sch-6-sec-24a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "24A Decision by the Attorney-General to refuse consent to transfer",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 23,
      "values:originalText": "to Australia\n(1) The Attorney-General may decide to refuse consent to the transfer\nof a prisoner to Australia under this Part:\n(a) after the Attorney-General receives a request under\nsection 24 for the transfer; but\n(b) before the Attorney-General has started to act under any of\nsections 26 to 32 in relation to the transfer.\n(2) Sections 26 to 32 do not apply for the transfer of the prisoner if the\nAttorney-General decides under subsection (1) of this section to\nrefuse consent to the transfer."
    },
