    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023-sch-9-sec-29a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "29A Past program participants",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023#sch-9-sec-29a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023.pdf, p.27",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to a person (a past program participant) who:\n(a) was, at some time before the commencement of this Act,\nincluded in a program (the past program) operated by the\nAustralian Federal Police for the purpose of witness\nprotection before the commencement of this Act; but\n(b) was not included in the past program immediately before the\ncommencement of this Act.\nNote 1:\nThis Act commenced on 18 April 1995.\nNote 2:\nThe transitional provision in subsection 29(2) applies to people who\nwere included in the past program immediately before the\ncommencement of this Act.\n(2) For the purposes of this Act:\n(a) a past program participant is taken to be a former participant;\nand\n(b) an identity provided to a past program participant under the\npast program is taken to have been provided under the\nNWPP.\n(3) To avoid doubt, paragraph (2)(a) does not prevent a past program\nparticipant from becoming included in the NWPP under this Act.\n\nSchedule 9  Witness protection",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies to a person (a past program participant) who:\n(a) was, at some time before the commencement of this Act,\nincluded in a program (the past program) operated by the\nAustralian Federal Police for the purpose of witness\nprotection before the commencement of this Act; but\n(b) was not included in the past program immediately before the\ncommencement of this Act.\nNote 1:\nThis Act commenced on 18 April 1995.\nNote 2:\nThe transitional provision in subsection 29(2) applies to people who\nwere included in the past program immediately before the\ncommencement of this Act.\n(2) For the purposes of this Act:\n(a) a past program participant is taken to be a former participant;\nand\n(b) an identity provided to a past program participant under the\npast program is taken to have been provided under the\nNWPP.\n(3) To avoid doubt, paragraph (2)(a) does not prevent a past program\nparticipant from becoming included in the NWPP under this Act.\n\nSchedule 9  Witness protection",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023-sch-9-sec-29a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023-sch-9-sec-29a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023-sch-9-sec-29a-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "217eb5c1e0d6c99605d8d271fac723ef76f273ebeb592796af743bd074f980f5"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023#sch-9-sec-29a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "29A Past program participants",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 27,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to a person (a past program participant) who:\n(a) was, at some time before the commencement of this Act,\nincluded in a program (the past program) operated by the\nAustralian Federal Police for the purpose of witness\nprotection before the commencement of this Act; but\n(b) was not included in the past program immediately before the\ncommencement of this Act.\nNote 1:\nThis Act commenced on 18 April 1995.\nNote 2:\nThe transitional provision in subsection 29(2) applies to people who\nwere included in the past program immediately before the\ncommencement of this Act.\n(2) For the purposes of this Act:\n(a) a past program participant is taken to be a former participant;\nand\n(b) an identity provided to a past program participant under the\npast program is taken to have been provided under the\nNWPP.\n(3) To avoid doubt, paragraph (2)(a) does not prevent a past program\nparticipant from becoming included in the NWPP under this Act.\n\nSchedule 9  Witness protection"
    },
