    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023-sch-9-sec-17c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "17C Review of decision to suspend protection and assistance",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023#sch-9-sec-17c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023.pdf, p.31",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to a decision under subsection 17B(1) to\nsuspend the protection and assistance provided to a participant\nunder the NWPP (a suspension decision), other than such a\ndecision made as a result of a review under this section.\n(2) A participant who receives notification of a suspension decision\nmay, within 7 days after receiving the notification, apply in writing\nto the Commissioner for a review of the decision.\n(3) If an application is made, the Commissioner:\n(a) must review the decision, and confirm, reverse or vary it; and\n(b) before making that decision, must give the participant a\nreasonable opportunity to state the participant’s case; and\n(c) after making that decision, must inform the participant in\nwriting of the decision.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies to a decision under subsection 17B(1) to\nsuspend the protection and assistance provided to a participant\nunder the NWPP (a suspension decision), other than such a\ndecision made as a result of a review under this section.\n(2) A participant who receives notification of a suspension decision\nmay, within 7 days after receiving the notification, apply in writing\nto the Commissioner for a review of the decision.\n(3) If an application is made, the Commissioner:\n(a) must review the decision, and confirm, reverse or vary it; and\n(b) before making that decision, must give the participant a\nreasonable opportunity to state the participant’s case; and\n(c) after making that decision, must inform the participant in\nwriting of the decision.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023-sch-9-sec-17c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023-sch-9-sec-17c-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023-sch-9-sec-17c-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1010c62b8906d4b853322c90bd61d0932f09999ef06f1e42fa696879b0b5a7dc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023#sch-9-sec-17c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "17C Review of decision to suspend protection and assistance",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 31,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to a decision under subsection 17B(1) to\nsuspend the protection and assistance provided to a participant\nunder the NWPP (a suspension decision), other than such a\ndecision made as a result of a review under this section.\n(2) A participant who receives notification of a suspension decision\nmay, within 7 days after receiving the notification, apply in writing\nto the Commissioner for a review of the decision.\n(3) If an application is made, the Commissioner:\n(a) must review the decision, and confirm, reverse or vary it; and\n(b) before making that decision, must give the participant a\nreasonable opportunity to state the participant’s case; and\n(c) after making that decision, must inform the participant in\nwriting of the decision."
    },
